definitions.construction:
Fix once and for all a finite number of folds and a deterministic fold assignment.  Partition \([0,1]\) into half-open bins of width \(b_n\asymp(\log n/n)^{1/(5+\kappa_+)}\), with the last bin closed at one.  On each training fold and bin, estimate \(g\) by the minimum-norm solution of
\[
 \sum_i\mathbf 1_i X_iB_iB_i^{\mathsf T}\widehat\theta_{g,j}
 =\sum_i\mathbf 1_iB_iA_i,
\]
and estimate \(\mu_1\) and \(\mu_0\) by the analogous treatment- and control-weighted local-linear least-squares equations.  If a displayed Gram matrix is singular, use the fixed fallback coefficient giving \(g=\varepsilon\) or \(\mu_a=1/2\), respectively.  Clip the fitted functions to the primitive bounds, impose \(x\widehat g(x)\leq1-\varepsilon\), and set \(\widehat e(x)=x\widehat g(x)\).  For held-out unit \(i\), let \(\widehat D_i=1+(\delta_n-1)\widehat e_i\) and
\[
\begin{split}
 \widehat\varphi_{\delta_n,i}={}&
 \frac{A_i\delta_n\{Y_i-\widehat\mu_{1,i}\}}{\widehat D_i}
 +\frac{(1-A_i)\{Y_i-\widehat\mu_{0,i}\}}{\widehat D_i}
 +\frac{\delta_n(\widehat\mu_{1,i}-\widehat\mu_{0,i})(A_i-\widehat e_i)}{\widehat D_i^2}\\
 &+\widehat\mu_{0,i}
 +\frac{\delta_n\widehat e_i(\widehat\mu_{1,i}-\widehat\mu_{0,i})}{\widehat D_i},
\end{split}
\]
where every fitted value is trained off the fold containing \(i\).  Set \(\widehat\psi_{\delta_n}=n^{-1}\sum_{i=1}^n\widehat\varphi_{\delta_n,i}\).  Thus the construction is a measurable total map even on singular training samples; the fallback is used only on the vanishing Gram-failure event.
